<title>BELGIUM: Germany's Waigel reserves right for budget freeze.</title>
<headline>Germany's Waigel reserves right for budget freeze.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>German finance minister Theo Waigel said on Monday he was reserving the right to impose a freeze on government spending if required over the course of this year.</p>
<p>&quot;I reserve the right to a spending freeze for the rest of the year,&quot; Waigel told journalists after meeting other EU finance ministers in Brussels.</p>
<p>He added that the finance ministry would also pay close attention to ensure that government expenditure did not run over planned limits in the run-up to European monetary union qualification, to be determined early next year.</p>
</text>
